From: Beniamino Galvani <bgalvani@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 19:21:02 +0200
Subject: dbus: Fix reporting of the SAE KeyMgmt

Not all drivers report SAE in the supported AKMs. Also check flag
NL80211_FEATURE_SAE (mapped to WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_SAE) to detect support
for SAE in the D-Bus KeyMgmt capabilities, similarly to what ctrl_iface
and dpp_supplicant already do.

Signed-off-by: Beniamino Galvani <bgalvani@redhat.com>
Origin: upstream, https://w1.fi/cgit/hostap/commit/?id=26c7f1bc107843f0ae57d35f3c9363367a0d11e7
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1147955
Bug: https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux/issues/7528
---
 wpa_supplicant/dbus/dbus_new_handlers.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/wpa_supplicant/dbus/dbus_new_handlers.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/dbus/dbus_new_handlers.c
@@ -3169,7 +3169,8 @@ dbus_bool_t wpas_dbus_getter_capabilities(
 #endif /* CONFIG_WPS */
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_SAE
-		if ((capa.key_mgmt & WPA_DRIVER_CAPA_KEY_MGMT_SAE) &&
+		if (((capa.key_mgmt & WPA_DRIVER_CAPA_KEY_MGMT_SAE) ||
+		     (capa.flags & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_SAE)) &&
 		    !wpa_dbus_dict_string_array_add_element(&iter_array, "sae"))
 			goto nomem;
 #endif /* CONFIG_SAE */
